BT 14 TL 56 780 Td
/F2 15 Tf (The alignment part: three components that must match) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (An aligned course has three components.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (1. Intended learning outcomes \(ILOs\). Statements of what students should be able to do,) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (and at what level, as a result of learning. Each outcome contains a verb, for example) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf ("explain", "apply" or "design".) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (2. Teaching and learning activities \(TLAs\). The situations in which students practise) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (the verb of the outcome. If the outcome says "apply", students must spend time applying,) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (not only listening to someone who applies.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (3. Assessment tasks \(ATs\). Tasks that require students to perform the same verb, judged) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (against criteria that describe how well the outcome has been achieved.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (The verb is the link. It appears in the outcome, it is activated in the teaching and) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (learning activity, and it is demonstrated in the assessment task. When one of the three) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (components asks for a different verb, the system is misaligned.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf (A useful test is to write the three components in one table row and read the row aloud.) Tj T*
/F1 11 Tf (If the row does not sound like one coherent story, the course needs redesign.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 290 40 Td (3) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
